       into it, and read as a denser stripe under the links. With the bar
       transparent, the underline clearance argued below is no longer about
       what the bar hides, only about the controls not touching it. */
    background: transparent;
    /* BOTH HALVES OF THE 6px, and it takes both. `top` governs only where a
       sticky element STOPS once it is stuck; at rest the bar sits in normal
